# Keep it out of search engines and prevent public caching
<IfModule mod_headers.c>
  Header set X-Robots-Tag "noindex, nofollow, noarchive"
  Header set Cache-Control "no-store, no-cache, must-revalidate, private"
</IfModule>

# ============================================================================
# PASSWORD PROTECTION -- currently OFF. Turn it on before sharing this URL.
# ============================================================================
#
# WHAT THIS DOES AND DOES NOT PROTECT (read this part even if you skip setup)
#   This gates the PAGE -- the laid-out dashboard with zones, decision
#   support, trap signals, the position calculator. Once Basic Auth is on,
#   nobody without the password can load this HTML at all.
#
#   It does NOT gate the DATA underneath it. This page reads the same
#   Cloudflare Worker feed (live-market-status.itscreativeman04.workers.dev)
#   that the PUBLIC page at ../ also calls, and that Worker's GET endpoint
#   has no authentication of its own -- confirmed by reading
#   cloudflare/live_status_worker.js directly. Anyone who opens the public
#   page's network tab and copies that URL gets the exact same full JSON
#   this private page shows, Basic Auth or not.
#
#   Kumar decided (2026-08-07) to ship the page split first and the feed
#   split -- publishing a trimmed public payload and a separate full private
#   one -- later. This password protects against a casual visitor clicking
#   around the site. It does not protect against someone who thinks to check
#   the network tab. Treat that as still open until the feed is actually
#   split.
#
# SETUP -- one time, and you have to do it: I cannot create a password file,
# and you should never paste a password into a chat.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Easiest: hPanel -> Advanced -> Password Protect Directories, pointed at
#        public_html/mishra-ventures/live-market/my
#    That writes .htpasswd for you -- then skip to step 4.
#
#    To do it by hand instead, continue:
#
# 2. Create the password file OUTSIDE public_html so it can never be served:
#        /home/<your-user>/.htpasswd-livemarket
#    hPanel -> Files -> File Manager, or over FTP. Hostinger's password-protect
#    tool can generate the hashed line for you to paste in.
#
# 3. Uncomment the four lines below and set AuthUserFile to that FULL path.
#    A relative path will not work.
#
# 4. Test in a private window. You should get a browser password prompt
#    before any content appears at:
#        /mishra-ventures/live-market/my/
#    If it loads with no prompt, it is still public.
#
# Reuse the SAME .htpasswd file as the discipline journal
# (../../discipline-journal/my/.htpasswd) if you want one password for both
# private pages instead of a second one to remember.

#AuthType Basic
#AuthName "Live Market — Private"
#AuthUserFile /home/REPLACE-WITH-YOUR-USER/.htpasswd-livemarket
#Require valid-user
